abstract: 'The Gaia DR3 wide-binary catalog tests whether weak-field velocity excesses
  are better described as smooth Temporal Shear recovery in TEP. From 341,315 high-purity
  systems, the analysis identifies a screening transition at R_s = 2,646 ± 182 AU
  (±609 AU total), strongly preferred under diagonal, AR(1) and Gaussian-process covariance
  treatments (covariance-aware Δχ² ≥ 1,073 against flat Newtonian; ≥ 284 against constant
  boost), with outer orbits saturating at alpha_sat = 0.366 ± 0.012 above the Keplerian
  baseline. The signal shows the environmental ordering required by TEP; Newtonian
  forward models do not reproduce the observed outer plateau.

  '
title: 'Temporal Equivalence Principle: Temporal Shear Recovery in Gaia DR3 Wide Binaries'
